/** \file klip.dox
 * \brief User's Guide for Karhunen-Loeve Image Processing and klipReduce.
 */

/** \addtogroup klipreduce_user_guide
 * @{
 *
 * `klipReduce` performs Karhunen-Loeve Image Processing (KLIP) on configured annular regions. It reads the common
 * hciReduce input sequence, constructs a reference library for each target image, estimates a PSF from retained KL
 * modes, subtracts it, then applies the common ADI derotation and final-combination stages.
 *
 * \section klip_modes Run modes
 *
 * `basic` and `normal` run a configured reduction. `postprocess` reads saved PSF-subtracted products and reapplies
 * the currently configured post-median, derotation, and combination stages. For `postprocess`, set
 * `postprocess.directory`, `postprocess.prefix`, and `postprocess.extension`.
 *
 * \section klip_regions Regions and KL modes
 *
 * `geom.minRadius` and `geom.maxRadius` define matching radial bounds. Optional `geom.minAngle` and
 * `geom.maxAngle` split them into wedges; omitted angle vectors mean full annuli. `klip.Nmodes` is the ordered list
 * of requested retained KL modes and therefore sets the output-cube planes.
 * These KLIP-specific settings may be omitted when `preProcess.only=true`; that mode stops after the shared input and
 * preprocessing pipeline.
 *
 * `adi.excludeMethod`, `adi.minDPx`, and `adi.maxDPx` control which ADI frames may enter each target's reference
 * library. `klip.includeMethod` and `klip.includeRefNum` provide explicit inclusion controls. `klip.rightReason`
 * and `klip.rrRadius` enable the specialized right-reason diagnostic/projection path.
 *
 * \section klip_psf_response PSF responses
 *
 * KLIP normally measures a centered PSF template at a small polar grid instead of densely probing every image pixel.
 * Configure `psfResponse.file`, an odd `psfResponse.stampSize`, exactly one of explicit
 * `psfResponse.sampleRadii` or positive `psfResponse.radiiPerRegion`, and exactly one positive angular control.
 * `psfResponse.samplesPerRadius` fixes the count at every radius; `psfResponse.sampleArcStep` instead resolves the
 * minimum count whose circular arc spacing is no larger than the configured pixel distance. The source locations are
 * exact uniformly spaced sky-frame coordinates. A positive `psfResponse.sampleAvoidRadius` omits locations near
 * configured `planet.*` coordinates and fails if a radial node has no remaining sample.
 *
 * `psfResponse.method=skyExact`, the default, inverse-rotates each probe into the target detector frame, applies the
 * supported regional centering, projects through the frozen target-specific basis, and accumulates directly into a
 * compact derotated stamp. Frame stamps use the configured science combination rule and weights, except that active
 * science `sigmaMean` is mapped to an unclipped mean for the analytic response. Mean and weighted-mean responses are
 * linear frozen-basis products. Median remains a response-template approximation rather than a finite-amplitude-
 * independent transfer function.
 *
 * `psfResponse.method=refitDifference` includes KL-basis adaptation numerically. For every retained location, KLIP
 * injects the unnormalized post-preprocessing template at positive and negative `psfResponse.refitContrast`, reruns
 * the complete regional fit and final combination without writing trial products, and divides the final-image
 * difference by twice that half-amplitude. The ordinary science cube is restored and processed normally after the
 * paired trials. This path costs two complete KLIP reductions per retained location and currently supports ADI only;
 * it is the validated numerical reference for a future analytic eigenmode-derivative implementation.
 *
 * Set `psfResponse.sampleEveryPixel=true` instead of all radial and angular controls to retain the paired response
 * independently at every eligible integer search pixel. This mode does not rotate, average, or interpolate the
 * measured responses. It requires `sampleAvoidRadius=0`, writes schema-2 `PIXEL_EXACT` coordinates, response, and
 * validity products, and is intended as a full numerical oracle rather than the production-cost estimator. A
 * signal-free oracle can first put a fitted positive source in `[planet]` and set `fake.subtractPlanet=true`; the
 * paired trials then measure `(KLIP(D-Pbest+epsilon Pxy)-KLIP(D-Pbest-epsilon Pxy))/(2 epsilon)`.
 *
 * Measurements at a common radius are rotated to the positive-column direction and averaged. Arbitrary radii linearly
 * blend the bracketing averages, using only stamp samples valid in both radial endpoints; requests outside the
 * sampled interval use the nearest endpoint. Nodes generated by `radiiPerRegion` and all subsequent interpolation
 * remain within their owning reduction region. Product provenance records the measurement method, region model,
 * configured science estimator, effective analytic-response estimator, avoidance radius, and paired trial count.
 * For `skyExact`, mean and weighted-mean response contributions are accumulated in worker-local sums, so their
 * retained response storage scales with the OpenMP worker count rather than the number of target frames. Median
 * response combination retains the per-frame stamps needed by that nonlinear estimator. FITS provenance identifies
 * `WORKER_SUM`, `FRAME_STACK`, or `PAIRED_FINAL_DIFFERENCE` accumulation and records the retained response bytes
 * excluding container overhead.
 * Set `psfResponse.filter=true` to evaluate the radial model, or select the retained exact response, at each science
 * pixel and apply the signed normalized
 * matched filter `sum(H I) / sum(H^2)`. The filtered amplitude cube is written beside the final science image;
 * response-energy normalization, usable-stamp support, validity, and a completion manifest are written in the
 * final image's `_outputs` directory. `psfResponse.filterMinGoodFract` controls the minimum retained stamp fraction.
 *
 * The response implementation supports complete, non-overlapping annuli, `none` or `imageMean` centering, no
 * pixel time-series normalization, enabled derotation and final combination, and no post-median subtraction. Median
 * centering, RMS normalization, wedges, and post-median subtraction are rejected because their perturbation or
 * region-boundary response has not yet been defined. `psfResponse.outputModels=true` writes one canonical radial
 * response cube and one validity cube per configured mode, or the schema-2 per-pixel products, in the final image's
 * `_outputs` directory.
 *
 * The implementation automatically forms the smaller of the reference-image and pixel-space covariance matrices for
 * each realized library. This is an internal performance optimization: it preserves configured mode order and the
 * reduction interface, while making narrow regions with many reference images substantially faster.
 * The direct KLIP calculation uses a fixed M32D64 policy: regional and covariance arithmetic is FP32 and the
 * covariance is promoted for an FP64 eigensolve. This is not a configuration choice. The opt-in exact
 * factor-deletion solver remains FP64 internally before returning modes to FP32 storage.
 *
 * \section klip_diagnostics Diagnostics
 *
 * Set `klip.writeDiagnostics=true` and choose `klip.diagnosticDirectory` to write region and reference-library
 * diagnostics. These products help audit frame selection and geometry; they do not change the science result.
 *
 * \section klip_dictionary Configuration reference
 *
 * See the \ref klip_configuration_dictionary "klipReduce configuration dictionary" for every application, geometry,
 * library-selection, PCA, and diagnostic option. Shared input, preprocessing, ADI, combination, and output settings
 * are documented in the \ref common_configuration_dictionary "common dictionary".
 *
 * @}
 */
